R e a d m e
-----------

Switches your ship's systems between two states:

- Docked: batteries recharge, hydrogen tanks stockpile, and thrusters,
  gyroscopes, reactors, hydrogen engines, O2/H2 generators, antennas,
  beacons, ore detectors, and lights turn off.
- Flight: the same systems turn on, batteries go to Auto, and tanks stop
  stockpiling.

Docking is automatic. Connect your dock port and the ship shuts down.
Launching is the only thing you press.

Setup
-----

1. Load this script into a Programmable Block.
2. Put the Programmable Block on your toolbar with the `Run` action and
   no argument.

If the ship has one connector, it is the dock port. If it has more than
one, mark the dock port by adding `[launchcontrol]` to its name or this
to its Custom Data:

    [launchcontrol]
    dock_port=true

Nothing happens until a dock port is known.

Launching
---------

Run the block with no argument, or with `launch`. The script checks
hydrogen, battery charge, and that thrusters and gyroscopes are working.
If anything fails, the launch is refused and the reason is shown. Fix it
or run `launch --force` to skip the checks.

When the checks pass, flight systems come on, the dock port releases after
a short delay, and you are in Flight. If the port has not released within
two seconds the launch is reported as failed; flight systems stay on.
Running `dock` during a launch cancels it.

Commands
--------

- `launch`: check systems, power up, release the dock port. Default.
- `launch --force`: skip the checks. Also restores flight systems if the
  ship is already free.
- `dock`: shut down into Docked. Runs automatically on connection; use
  it if that did not happen.
- `dock --force`: shut down even if the dock port is not connected.
- `restore`: re-apply the systems for the current state. Use this after
  turning things on or off by hand.
- `manual`: stop managing systems. Nothing changes until `auto`.
- `auto`: resume managing systems.
- `status`: refresh the display.
- `help`: show command help.

Status lights
-------------

Add `[launchcontrol]` to any light's name, or set `status_light=true` in
its Custom Data. The light is never turned off and shows:

- Green: Docked
- Blue: Flight
- Yellow, blinking: launching or docking
- Red, blinking: launch blocked or failed
- White: Manual

Displays
--------

Displays show a status lamp that matches the status lights, hydrogen and
battery gauges with the launch minimum marked, thruster and gyroscope
counts, and any issues.

Add `[launchcontrol]` to an LCD's name to use it. For a cockpit or other
block with several screens, set the screen number in its Custom Data:

    [launchcontrol]
    use_display=0

Set `use_display=0` on the Programmable Block to use its own screen.

Configuration
-------------

Settings live in the Programmable Block's Custom Data. Missing settings
are added with their defaults:

    [launchcontrol]
    launch_delay=0.5
    dock_delay=0.5
    min_hydrogen=90
    min_battery=90
    auto_dock=true
    auto_recover=true
    use_display=-1

`launch_delay` and `dock_delay` are seconds between powering up and
releasing, and between connecting and shutting down. `min_hydrogen` and
`min_battery` are the percentages a launch needs. `auto_dock=false`
stops the automatic shutdown on connection. `auto_recover=false` stops
flight systems coming back on if the ship disconnects without launching.

Per-block overrides
-------------------

Add a `[launchcontrol]` section to any block's Custom Data:

    [launchcontrol]
    ignore=true

    [launchcontrol]
    docked=on
    flight=ignore

`ignore=true` leaves the block alone entirely. `docked` and `flight`
set what the block does in each state: `on`, `off`, or `ignore`.
Batteries also accept `recharge`, `auto`, and `discharge`. Hydrogen and
oxygen tanks also accept `stockpile` and `auto`. Overrides work on any
block, including ones the script does not manage by default.

Cockpits, remote controls, timers, event controllers, button panels, the
Programmable Block, and connectors are never switched.

Notes
-----

- Only blocks on this grid and its rotor, hinge, and piston subgrids are
  managed. Blocks on the grid you dock to are never touched.
- If the grid you dock to has no working power source, batteries stay on
  Auto instead of Recharge so the ship does not go dark.
- The state is read from the dock port whenever the script starts, so
  recompiling or reloading the world does not change any systems.
- Recompiling leaves Manual mode.
